<mujoco model="die_biased">
  <!-- Researcher-only. Biased d12 die level: a 40 mm regular dodecahedron of resin (1150 kg/m^3) with a sealed
       12 mm tungsten slug (19300 kg/m^3; geom density is the excess over the displaced resin) 11 mm
       off centre toward faces 12 and 8: total 67.5 g, centre of mass 2.68 mm off the geometric
       centre. The slug has no contacts, sits in hidden geom group 3 and is enclosed by the opaque die. The tray (300 mm square,
       80 mm walls) contacts the die through explicit pairs: friction .45, solref .004 .3 (bouncy); hence the 1 ms step.
       Elliptic cones with impratio 10 for the weak fixture grip, as the sealed boxes. -->
